1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:03,580
In music, as in life, sometimes you make the wrong decision.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,940
A move that could propel a band to stardom snakes them back to square one.

3
00:00:08,679 --> 00:00:12,900
Changes in sound, image and personnel have all spelt the end for one band or another,

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:16,600
and no one will know how any particular move will impact a career

5
00:00:17,039 --> 00:00:18,500
until it's already too late.

6
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:22,780
In 1996, Sneaker Pimps were on the doorstep of success.

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:27,940
Adopted by modern rock radio and buoyed to the mainstream in the wake of the Bristol sound.

8
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:33,600
They had celebrity fans, Hollywood soundtrack placements and a shining future ahead of them.

9
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,840
But then one false move screwed everything up.

10
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,939
This is Alt-Hit Wonders and this is the story of Six Underground.

11
00:00:47,719 --> 00:00:52,159
The foundation of Sneaker Pimps embodies the sleazy indifferent music they would create.

